WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
Nusumareta kako wo

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
Sagashitsuzukete

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Ore wa samayou

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
Mishiranu machi wo

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Honou no nioi shimitsuite

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Museru

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Sayonara wa itta hazu da

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
Wakareta hazu sa

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
Jigoku wo mireba

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
Kokoro ga kawaku

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Tatakai wa akita no sa

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
Sadame to areba

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Kokoro wo kimeru

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
Sottoshite oite kure

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Ashita ni

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Aa tsunagaru kyou gurai

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.290
At this rate, Chirico's going to die.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:49.420
I've given him the best treatment I can.

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:51.750
I can't do anything more here.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:01.210
Ypsilon

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:11.000
Their being in the Non-aggression Zone
doesn't matter!

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:12.290
I mean it!

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:14.750
We have to go after that ship and capture it!

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:16.960
You'd ignore the cease-fire?!

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:18.790
You think the Gilgamesh would stand for that?!

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:20.130
That's beside the point!

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:21.960
We can't ignore the existence of a Perfect Soldier!

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:24.080
You'd restart the war!

00:02:24.420 --> 00:02:26.000
Then it'd just be a question of us winning!

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.960
The existence of the PS is a major threat!

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:30.210
Exactly my point!

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:34.830
If the Gilgamesh have perfected them,
we have to avoid war at all costs!

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:37.790
There are only two PSs on that ship!

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.210
We may not know why,
but they're definitely fugitives!

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:43.830
The problem is we still don't know
where the ship came from.

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:47.330
But their being in the Zone leaves us one option.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:50.750
We have to hide our presence there.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.040
And we have to wait and see what happens.

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:03.580
Captain, our orders are to just follow them.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:04.670
No matter!

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:06.960
If we capture them, we'll be heroes!

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:12.380
Stop that! You know what happened to
the guys we sent out before.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:15.000
The people on that ship aren't normal humans.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.170
Chirico...

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:26.920
I've made up my mind.

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:30.290
This is the only way to save you.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:33.330
To them, I'm an invaluable PS.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:40.830
Yes... A PS!

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:56.040
Chirico... Wait for me!

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:37.500
The glory of our Society is eternal.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:40.330
Whoever isn't a part of it is our enemy.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:43.170
That which invites misfortune must be eradicated.

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:46.420
Destroy that ship, and Chirico along with it!

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:47.790
And what about Proto One?

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:52.540
Hmm... She is invaluable, being the first PS.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:55.420
But we must maintain secrecy,

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:59.040
and can't afford to let even her
dead body fall into enemy hands.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:01.580
We'll have to get her back!

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:02.540
Sir!

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:05.630
Move out at once! That is all!

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:09.790
Lay in a pursuit course! Full speed ahead!

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:11.290
Pursuit course, ahead full!

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:13.790
Aye, aye! Pursuit course, engines ahead full!

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:36.330
Emotion Index: Up 52.46

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.960
Pulse data B: 1, 5, 1.4

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:43.290
Body temperature, I-group: 7, 3, 6

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:50.540
Chirico and Ypsilon's showdown
is fast approaching.

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:54.710
Ah, yes. When Ypsilon's hatred will be at its peak.

00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:58.630
But you still believe this
Hatred Index can be changed?

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:00.040
I believe so.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:05.670
Borough theorized that a PS would reach its
full potential at an even higher level than this.

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:09.920
I'm interested in whether it will change
after he's killed Chirico.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:14.000
True, true. That is the main point
of this experiment after all.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:24.630
This is radar section.

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:28.330
A small craft has launched
from the unidentified ship.

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:30.330
On course for the pursuing Balarant vessel.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:31.290
What?!

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.880
Visual coming through.

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:37.250
Range: 10,000 and closing.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.580
Monitor any transmissions!

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:54.670
What's it doing?

00:06:55.250 --> 00:06:57.330
Doesn't look like it's going to attack us.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:07:00.330
That's a PS out there! Don't get careless!

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:02.420
It's probably trying to give us a message.

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:04.040
Hail it.

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:09.290
...not open fire!

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.670
Please do not open fire!

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:13.670
This is the PS from the ship.

00:07:13.670 --> 00:07:16.080
Please do not open fire!

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:19.210
The... The PS! It's a woman?!

00:07:19.210 --> 00:07:20.960
I don't believe it!

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:24.830
This is Leslion launch #3, Balarant forces.

00:07:24.830 --> 00:07:27.000
Are you the only PS, Miss?

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:28.460
Respond!

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:32.580
Yes, I'm the only PS. I surrender!

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:34.290
I ask only one condition.

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:37.880
There's a severely wounded soldier
still onboard the ship.

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:40.170
Just one PS?!

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:43.880
You mean the other one who fought
our ATs WASN'T a Perfect Soldier?!

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:45.920
Roger. I'm the only one.

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:49.540
I can't believe that,
especially after seeing him fight!

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:51.380
We'll know when we investigate.

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:53.500
What do you want us to do?

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:56.130
The wounded soldier on the ship
is hurt very badly.

00:07:56.130 --> 00:07:57.460
He can't be moved.

00:07:57.750 --> 00:07:59.330
I'll surrender.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:01.130
In return, you won't capture Chirico-

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:03.420
The soldier, I mean. Please!

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:06.790
He'll be taken care of,
provided you really are a PS.

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:08.420
Prepare to be taken aboard.

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:11.000
You may dock at your leisure.

00:08:11.790 --> 00:08:14.380
Lady Luck must be smiling upon us.

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:36.000
Wh-who?!

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:44.000
Source of intercepted transmission: Proto One!

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:48.040
Fool! That's what you get for trying to be clever!

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:50.170
We got part of the transmission on tape!

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:51.040
Play it back.

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:51.920
Yes, sir!

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:55.250
Yes, I'm the only PS. I surrender!

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:57.710
The wounded soldier on the ship
is hurt very badly.

00:08:57.710 --> 00:08:59.420
He can't be moved.

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:01.460
Proto One!

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:04.130
I'll surrender.

00:09:04.130 --> 00:09:05.880
In return, you won't capture Chirico-

00:09:05.880 --> 00:09:08.380
the soldier, I mean. Please!

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:10.830
He'll be taken care of,
provided you really are a PS.

00:09:12.210 --> 00:09:13.210
That's all we got.

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:17.540
Proto One was a hairsbreadth away
from falling into Balarant hands.

00:09:21.130 --> 00:09:24.920
Psycron excitement data: Up 8.6

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:28.080
The highest level yet.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:33.750
We have Chirico's ship on video.

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:34.630
Show it!

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:35.380
Yes, sir!

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:29.330
You came back.

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:31.040
You knew?

00:10:32.580 --> 00:10:33.540
Yeah.

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:39.210
I went to their ship,
to turn myself over to the Balarant...

00:10:39.210 --> 00:10:40.710
Why did you come back?

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:43.420
Their ship was destroyed.

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:45.500
The Teltain attacked it.

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:47.500
The Teltain?!

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:15.630
That was... that was the ship I was on!

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:18.920
The Teltain's coming!

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:20.830
The ship that ruined my life!

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:23.630
I'll kill them! Kill their whole damned Society!

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:25.330
No! Don't move!

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:27.330
Stop it! Stop trying to fight them!

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:30.210
I have to! My destiny is to fight!

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:32.460
Chirico!

00:11:44.790 --> 00:11:47.040
Just sleep for now.

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:49.040
I won't let you die...

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:51.670
Even if that costs me my life!

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:19.380
Captain, do we launch an AT attack right now?

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:23.960
Don't be rash. We'll see how well
a barrage will do against them.

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:27.170
Sir! Commencing long-range barrage at once!

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:29.790
Prepare to fire on that ship!

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.330
Aye, sir! Targeting weaponry
on the unidentified ship.

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:38.080
Targetting data - Range: 85,000 to bow!

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:40.420
Elevation: 25 degrees!

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:42.250
Deflection: 35 degrees to port!

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:10.540
Ypsilon! Ypsilon, come in!

00:13:25.750 --> 00:13:27.170
Cease fire!

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:28.580
Cease fire!

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:35.170
Launch AT team!

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:37.580
We should wait until it lands!

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:41.290
They have no way to attack us.

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:43.420
We'll finish them off here and now!

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:46.580
You underestimate Chirico at your own peril, sir!

00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:49.210
That's not for you to say!

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:51.080
AT team, launch!

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:53.460
Aye, sir! AT team, launch!

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:13.210
Valerie team, launching!

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:24.330
His clinical responses are excellent.

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:28.540
I thought Ypsilon would leave
to steal Proto One back immediately.

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:31.130
He wants to verify Chirico's condition.

00:14:31.130 --> 00:14:34.920
I wonder if Chirico really is
too badly injured to fight.

00:14:34.920 --> 00:14:38.710
Well, being on the ground will limit
their actions to only two dimensions.

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:40.790
And we have them outnumbered.

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:43.080
I'll wait for when Ypsilon goes out.

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:44.040
It's starting.

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:54.540
Where's Ypsilon?

00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:18.210
They've launched an AT against us?

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:22.170
Captain, it looks like Proto One
is fighting by herself.

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:25.380
She's asking that Ypsilon be sent out to her.

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:27.540
Why would she do that?!

00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:32.080
I'm going out!

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:33.830
Put my personal AT team on stand-by!

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:36.420
Put Ypsilon's team on stand-by!

00:17:10.290 --> 00:17:11.580
Proto One...

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:22.330
So, Chirico can't move?

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:24.710
He's hurt badly.

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:26.250
I have a favor to ask.

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:29.330
Then ask it.

00:17:31.630 --> 00:17:33.500
Let me guess.

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:38.330
You want us to spare Chirico
if you return to the Society.

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:41.210
Please! Just let him live!

00:17:41.210 --> 00:17:43.130
I don't care what happens to me!

00:17:43.130 --> 00:17:44.380
I'll do whatever you want.

00:17:44.380 --> 00:17:45.630
Is that all you have to say?

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:49.250
Yes! Just spare Chirico and-

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:50.250
Shut up!

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:53.290
I owe no favors to the one who cast me into Hell!

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:56.710
Now, Proto One. Come to me.

00:17:57.250 --> 00:18:00.420
No! I won't abandon Chirico!

00:18:00.420 --> 00:18:02.170
You WILL come back with me!

00:18:05.080 --> 00:18:06.330
Don't shoot!

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:08.250
I'll do it!

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:33.170
Chirico!

00:18:38.710 --> 00:18:40.000
Fyana...

00:18:53.540 --> 00:18:55.080
Open fire!

00:19:06.670 --> 00:19:07.630
Chirico!

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:12.500
Captain, Proto One's...!

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:17.040
Proto One, come back!

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:18.580
All units, move in!

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:22.040
Cease fire!

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:23.790
Cease fire!

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:25.250
That god damned...!

00:19:25.580 --> 00:19:29.580
His Love Index for Proto One
has exceeded his Hatred Index.

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:33.130
Definitely a defect, having a PS so easily moved.

00:19:33.130 --> 00:19:34.580
That's uncertain.

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:37.040
When Chirico's taken care of,
we'll reestablish our control.

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:39.250
I'll be interested in seeing that change.

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:43.500
Spread out and search! Find Chirico!

00:21:13.040 --> 00:21:14.040
Get her!

00:21:31.130 --> 00:21:32.210
Fyana!

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:33.540
Chirico...

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:36.540
Looks like all we can do
is fight together until we die.

00:21:36.540 --> 00:21:39.210
Forgive me, Chirico.

00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:40.670
I'll never leave you again.

00:21:40.670 --> 00:21:42.670
Will you fight with me until we're both dead?

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:44.540
No, we're going to live.

00:21:44.540 --> 00:21:46.920
If we fight together, I know we'll survive.

00:22:34.380 --> 00:22:37.330
My strength had mysteriously returned to me.

00:22:38.420 --> 00:22:40.790
But, as strong as Ypsilon's murderous rage was...

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:45.460
the smell of blood from
this planet's past was even stronger.

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.710
Next Episode

00:22:56.460 --> 00:23:01.330
At the extremes of love and hatred
lies hidden a murderous intent.

00:23:02.000 --> 00:23:04.960
But, when fully formed,
that intent isn't emotional.

00:23:04.960 --> 00:23:06.630
It is the product of cold-blooded logic.

00:23:07.130 --> 00:23:09.960
Man created this when he chose to play God.

00:23:10.210 --> 00:23:13.000
But what lies in God's mind?

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:14.880
Love? Or hatred?

00:23:15.540 --> 00:23:17.500
Next time, "Showdown"

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:20.420
Chirico will provoke God himself.

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:24.290
Showdown

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:24.290
Next Time

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:46.000
Samishii toki mo

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.540
Kanashii toki mo

00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:55.920
Itsumo anata ga me ni ukabu

00:23:56.420 --> 00:23:59.960
Hitori no toki mo

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:03.380
Aitai toki mo

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:09.630
Itsumo anata wa mune no naka

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:13.130
Tooku hanarete itemo

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:16.540
Tatoe wakarete itemo

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:23.040
Kono yo no hikari to tomo ni mabushiku

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:29.380
Ano hi no anata ga...
